From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:11:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Durable DB file storage, POPIA document erasure, server-side
 directory scoping

- storage: new 'db' backend (stored_files table in Postgres); STORAGE_BACKEND=auto resolves to db in
  production because Render's disk is wiped on every restart; legacy on-disk files are rescued into
  the DB on first read; already-lost files return a friendly 410 instead of a 500
- account deletion now deletes CV/generated-document bytes, wipes extracted CV text and generated
  content, and removes the candidate profile (POPIA right to erasure)
- /companies: country, q (LIKE-escaped) and ids filters; non-admin requests must be scoped (cap 1500,
  unscoped 100), 200/hour per account; new /companies/facets and /companies/surprise
- Companies page loads one slice at a time (cached); Career Agent fetches only what a question needs
- tests: storage backend, erasure, directory scoping; full suite green; Playwright e2e against a
  production-mode API with the full seed

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
